# Without this file, `docker build`/`podman build` sends every crate's
# `target/` directory into the build context before the `Dockerfile` gets a
# say — discovered while first verifying `Dockerfile`: the four crates it
# copies (`openehr`, `openehr-store`, `openehr-sqlite`, `openehr-loco`) carry
# a combined ~37 GB of local build artifacts on a machine that has run their
# test suites a few times, and a `COPY openehr ./openehr` with no exclusions
# copies all of it. `cargo build` inside the image cannot reuse a host
# `target/` built for the host's own toolchain and paths anyway, so this is
# pure transfer cost with no benefit.
**/target/
.git/
